From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 04:06:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 16/44] qwen27: one narrow-tape plane a seam, and no silent
 no-ops

The narrow tape shared the streams tape's plane count, so a seam id past that
count was silently dropped and a dump read an unwritten plane. Seams now get
their own slots from seam_base, a run declares which it wants, and completion
refuses when one never fired (IncompleteSeams). An unknown or out-of-range id is
an error rather than a skip.

With the tape trustworthy, the window measures 0.125 / cos 0.999979 at the fold
(same as the plain path) and 0.2889 rms against 0.2755 after enter, and the gate
reaches p1 64/64 and p2 64/64, p0 19/64 at a rank-2 near-tie.
